Cached the profile pointer and marked the null/out-of-range paths as unlikely, keeping the hot valid lookup as straight-line code. This avoids repeated member loads and improves branch layout.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumComponents(void) const
{
    const auto p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == NULL, 0))
        return 0;
    const auto idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect(idx >= p->numFields, 0))
        return 0;
    return p->fields[idx].numComponents;
}
```